TEXT 16 40 Left 3 ;STM32G431CBT6 running the FOC firmware: behavioural model of the code (a microcontroller has no SPICE model)
TEXT 32 96 Left 2 ;Pins are the real chip's. Inputs: ADC pins PA0 (phase A current), PA1 (phase B), PA2 (bus voltage); encoder angle and speed. Outputs: TIM1 PWM on PA8/PA9/PA10, driver enable PB0.
TEXT 32 136 Left 2 ;Each source below is one line of the firmware: its output node name is the variable, its expression is the code.
TEXT 64 260 Left 3 ;1 ADC READ: amps from the ADC counts
TEXT 1064 260 Left 3 ;2 ENCODER
TEXT 2064 260 Left 3 ;3 CLARKE + PARK (abc -> dq)
TEXT 3064 260 Left 3 ;4 SPEED LOOP -> iq command
TEXT 64 1260 Left 3 ;5 CURRENT LOOPS (PI + decoupling)
TEXT 1064 1260 Left 3 ;6 INVERSE PARK + CLARKE
TEXT 2064 1260 Left 3 ;7 SPACE-VECTOR DUTY
TEXT 3064 1260 Left 3 ;8 TIMER PWM OUT + DRIVER ENABLE
TEXT 64 2156 Left 3 ;THROTTLE (DShot from the flight controller), PWM CARRIER, BUS-VOLTAGE FILTER
TEXT 1364 2156 Left 3 ;SUPPLY CURRENT AND INPUT PINS (10 MOhm = pin leakage; ADC and encoder inputs are read by the code above)
